# S5 gitignore semantics.

# (a) A rule inside an excluded directory does NOT bring the file back. Git
#     never descends into an excluded folder, so BOTH files here are dropped,
#     including the one the ! names. This is the trap.
scripts/
!scripts/keep.sh

# (b) A leading slash anchors to the repo root.
/classes/A0.cls

# (c) A pattern containing a slash is anchored even without a leading one, and
#     a single * does not cross a directory separator. docs/a.md goes,
#     docs/sub/b.md stays.
docs/*.md

# (d) A trailing slash means directories only. There is a FILE called tmp at
#     the root; it must survive.
tmp/

# (e) Matching is case sensitive. classes/A00000.cls must survive this.
classes/a00000.cls
